{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00598",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.39,
      "end_seconds": 11.21,
      "duration_seconds": 10.82,
      "text": "I'm only here because the health visitor insisted. I've been a bit thirsty lately, that's all, it's nothing really."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 12.8,
      "end_seconds": 19.8,
      "duration_seconds": 7.0,
      "text": "Right, well I'm glad she did. How long has the thirst been going on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 21.48,
      "end_seconds": 30.66,
      "duration_seconds": 9.18,
      "text": "Two weeks, give or take. I just put it down to being up in the night with the baby."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 32.96,
      "end_seconds": 40.18,
      "duration_seconds": 7.22,
      "text": "Could be. Is it worse at any particular time, or all day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 41.11,
      "end_seconds": 48.87,
      "duration_seconds": 7.76,
      "text": "All day, really. I keep a bottle by the sofa. It's honestly fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 51.83,
      "end_seconds": 59.76,
      "duration_seconds": 7.93,
      "text": "Okay. Any blurred vision, with it? Print going fuzzy, that sort of thing?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 60.72,
      "end_seconds": 64.74,
      "duration_seconds": 4.02,
      "text": "No, my eyes are all right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 66.57,
      "end_seconds": 74.53,
      "duration_seconds": 7.96,
      "text": "Good. Let's go through what you're taking. Your notes say metformin, is that still right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 75.34,
      "end_seconds": 79.93,
      "duration_seconds": 4.59,
      "text": "Yes, metformin. 500 mg, twice a day, with food."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 82.5,
      "end_seconds": 85.45,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "Twice a day, every day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 86.42,
      "end_seconds": 88.4,
      "duration_seconds": 1.98,
      "text": "Every day, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 90.56,
      "end_seconds": 98.66,
      "duration_seconds": 8.1,
      "text": "Honestly, now. Most new mums miss some, and nobody will tell you off."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 101.55,
      "end_seconds": 111.82,
      "duration_seconds": 10.27,
      "text": "Well... the evening one, sometimes. When the baby's fussing at bedtime, it slips my mind. Maybe two or three nights a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 112.57,
      "end_seconds": 122.01,
      "duration_seconds": 9.44,
      "text": "Thank you, that's useful to know. I'm not worried by it, I just need the real picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 123.33,
      "end_seconds": 126.98,
      "duration_seconds": 3.65,
      "text": "It's not a big deal, is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 127.69,
      "end_seconds": 137.43,
      "duration_seconds": 9.74,
      "text": "It matters a little, which is why I'm asking. Your records also show you had gestational diabetes in your pregnancy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 139.49,
      "end_seconds": 146.96,
      "duration_seconds": 7.47,
      "text": "Yes, that's right. They told me it might go away after the birth."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 148.7,
      "end_seconds": 160.17,
      "duration_seconds": 11.47,
      "text": "It often does, but it can come back, which is why we recheck. And you've an underactive thyroid too, for about five years?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 163.07,
      "end_seconds": 168.5,
      "duration_seconds": 5.43,
      "text": "Five years, yes. That's all quiet, it never bothers me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 170.27,
      "end_seconds": 177.25,
      "duration_seconds": 6.98,
      "text": "Good. Let me take your blood pressure and check your weight on the scales."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 193.2,
      "end_seconds": 199.35,
      "duration_seconds": 6.15,
      "text": "Go on then. I've not dared step on them since the birth."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 201.69,
      "end_seconds": 207.89,
      "duration_seconds": 6.2,
      "text": "Blood pressure is 124/78. And your weight is 84 kg."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 210.82,
      "end_seconds": 214.27,
      "duration_seconds": 3.45,
      "text": "Eighty-four. Well, it could be worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 216.37,
      "end_seconds": 226.3,
      "duration_seconds": 9.93,
      "text": "That's no bad figure at all. Slip your shoes and socks off, I'll check your feet and ankles."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 228.4,
      "end_seconds": 233.33,
      "duration_seconds": 4.93,
      "text": "Do I have to? My feet are a state."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 248.91,
      "end_seconds": 254.19,
      "duration_seconds": 5.28,
      "text": "I've seen worse, I promise. Just let me look."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 256.7,
      "end_seconds": 263.81,
      "duration_seconds": 7.11,
      "text": "There's no swelling around the ankles, and the skin on your feet looks healthy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 265.32,
      "end_seconds": 267.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "Told you, nothing wrong."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 268.82,
      "end_seconds": 284.32,
      "duration_seconds": 15.5,
      "text": "So here are the options. One, we carry on as we are and do nothing more. Two, we check your sugar control with a blood test. Three, we change what you're taking."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 285.81,
      "end_seconds": 289.42,
      "duration_seconds": 3.61,
      "text": "Which one would you go for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 290.42,
      "end_seconds": 305.85,
      "duration_seconds": 15.43,
      "text": "The second. I'd like to arrange an HbA1c blood test, which shows your average sugar over the last few months. The nurse can do it before you leave."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 307.8,
      "end_seconds": 311.43,
      "duration_seconds": 3.63,
      "text": "Fine, if you think it's needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 313.48,
      "end_seconds": 320.55,
      "duration_seconds": 7.07,
      "text": "I do. Then we decide about the tablets once we have the number."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 321.79,
      "end_seconds": 324.45,
      "duration_seconds": 2.66,
      "text": "And if it's high?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 325.87,
      "end_seconds": 335.99,
      "duration_seconds": 10.12,
      "text": "Then we talk about options again: the dose, a different tablet, or more help with food and exercise. No decisions today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 337.04,
      "end_seconds": 344.58,
      "duration_seconds": 7.54,
      "text": "All right. Is it all right to keep taking the metformin meanwhile?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 345.46,
      "end_seconds": 359.4,
      "duration_seconds": 13.94,
      "text": "Yes, carry on with it, and try to build in the evening dose. Put it next to the baby's bottles, so you trip over it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 361.56,
      "end_seconds": 365.25,
      "duration_seconds": 3.69,
      "text": "That's actually clever. I'll do that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 367.48,
      "end_seconds": 376.62,
      "duration_seconds": 9.14,
      "text": "I'd like to see you again in three months, once the results are back and we've decided."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 378.87,
      "end_seconds": 383.37,
      "duration_seconds": 4.5,
      "text": "Three months. I'll put it in the calendar."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 385.09,
      "end_seconds": 395.96,
      "duration_seconds": 10.87,
      "text": "Reception will book it as you leave. Walking with the pram is a good start for exercise, by the way."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 397.06,
      "end_seconds": 404.19,
      "duration_seconds": 7.13,
      "text": "I do walk to the shops most days. The baby likes it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 407.11,
      "end_seconds": 414.47,
      "duration_seconds": 7.36,
      "text": "Then you're ahead of most. Keep drinking water for the thirst, rather than juice."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 416.53,
      "end_seconds": 420.43,
      "duration_seconds": 3.9,
      "text": "Right. Water only. Boring, but fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 422.98,
      "end_seconds": 433.6,
      "duration_seconds": 10.62,
      "text": "If the thirst gets much worse, or you start passing a lot more urine, ring us before the three months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 434.48,
      "end_seconds": 438.6,
      "duration_seconds": 4.12,
      "text": "I will, though I'm sure it won't."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 440.8,
      "end_seconds": 447.13,
      "duration_seconds": 6.33,
      "text": "Does your partner help at night, so you can get some sleep?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 448.88,
      "end_seconds": 455.4,
      "duration_seconds": 6.52,
      "text": "Some nights. He sleeps through the baby, it's almost a talent."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 456.74,
      "end_seconds": 463.96,
      "duration_seconds": 7.22,
      "text": "Ha. Then make him do the evening bottle, so you can rest. Any other questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 465.78,
      "end_seconds": 468.67,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "No, that's everything. Thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 471.23,
      "end_seconds": 477.12,
      "duration_seconds": 5.89,
      "text": "Good. Off you go, and congratulations on the little one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 479.48,
      "end_seconds": 482.65,
      "duration_seconds": 3.17,
      "text": "Thanks very much. Cheerio."
    }
  ]
}
